# Build artifacts — rebuildable from source, never committed.
# scripts/*/harness/target alone is ~1.2 GB of Rust intermediates.
target/
**/target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.dylib
*.so
*.a
*.d
*.timestamp

# Compiled task binaries — rebuilt by scripts/, see each system's BUILD.md.
tasks/*/bin/
*.test

# Cloned third-party provers are NEVER vendored here.
# Two of the five measured systems are licensed for evaluation only and
# explicitly forbid redistribution. Every script takes the prover from an
# environment variable pointing outside this tree. See each system's BUILD.md.
#
# NOTE: this list is deliberately NOT a set of bare directory names. Excluding
# by prover name would also silently delete `systems/<name>/` and
# `scripts/<name>/`, which are OUR documentation and OUR harnesses, not theirs.
# That exact mistake was made and caught before the first commit. The guarantee
# that no third-party source is here is enforced by an assertion in
# scripts/check-no-vendored-source.sh, not by these patterns.
vendor/
third_party/
clones/

# Harness manifests are GENERATED by each harness's setup.sh from its Cargo.toml.in,
# substituting the path to a prover clone that lives outside this tree. The materialised
# file therefore carries a machine-local absolute path and must never be committed; the
# template is what is committed.
scripts/*/harness/Cargo.toml

# Local noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.swp
